{"concept": "drv.motion.right_turn_from_onset", "state": "returned", "attempts": 1, "reasons": ["review: divergence 1 (fails_wrongly) at t=750 ms: With turn_angle set to zero, a second observed right-turn onset is itself a recognition observation. The body misses it because the heading-change comparison … — contract: holds, body: fails; contract: \"The act's observed beginning is the observation at which drv.motion.turning_right last became true. The act is …\" — upheld: In the executed facts turning_right falls at t=500 and rises again at t=750, so 750 is the new observed beginning. The heading change since it is 0, which reaches −0 first at 750, so the contract holds there. The body fails because its rising edge looks at the heading comparison, which was already true at t=500 when measured from the old onset; that is a wrong onset, not a choice of parameter size. — \"The act's observed beginning is the observation at which drv.motion.turning_right last became true. The act is recognized at the observation at which the heading change since that beginning first reaches the negative of the turn angle.\""], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_413_2"], "iteration": 1, "last_task": "results/smoke32-1111-2102/iter-001/code/concept__drv_motion_right_turn_from_onset", "judge_failures": {}, "waiting": [], "cost_failures": 0, "core_panics": 0, "held_laws": [], "scope_violations": 0}
